[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3302298756","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110570#issuecomment-3302298756","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110570","id":3302298756,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7E1RSE","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-17T10:13:13Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T10:16:27Z","body":"`WorldEnvironment` is a 3D specific node, and it is entirely dependent on other 3D code to work\n\nFor post-processing do you mean the compositor? The compositor is exclusive to the 3D pipeline.\n\nAs far as I can find none of the WorldEnvironment processing is relevant for 2D rendering, unless the tonemap system works for that\n\nSeparating this would probably require splitting the node into two parts, or somehow make the 3D only parts separate, but it entirely uses the 3D world code to handle things, which is not available in 3D disabled builds","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3302298756/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3303008000","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110570#issuecomment-3303008000","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110570","id":3303008000,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7E3-cA","user":{"login":"KerekesDavid","id":9087461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODc0NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9087461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid","html_url":"https://github.com/KerekesDavid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-17T13:25:04Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T13:48:35Z","body":"WorldEnvironment (or the ~equivalent Environment resource inside a World3D) afaik are the only way to get Glow, Tonemap, and Brigthness/Contrast/Saturation/LUT adjustments on a 2D game.\n\nCan confirm, it sets up at least some parts of a 3D pipeline to do this, which results in some overhead.\nThe amount of this overhead seems to differ from case to case, see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108935#issuecomment-3131572510 for an example that looks really bad on the profiler.\n\nNot sure how these screen space effects ended up in the 3D pipeline historically, but it is quite confusing that they are there, and they probably shouldn't be.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3303008000/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3306245244","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110570#issuecomment-3306245244","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110570","id":3306245244,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FEUx8","user":{"login":"sorascode","id":37141176,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MTQxMTc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37141176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sorascode","html_url":"https://github.com/sorascode","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sorascode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sorascode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sorascode/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sorascode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sorascode/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sorascode/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sorascode/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sorascode/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sorascode/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T08:37:01Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T08:37:01Z","body":"Yes, setting the Background Mode of the Environment resource to Canvas makes it work for 2D games.","author_association":"NONE","pin":n